WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.940
Configuration management is the process of establishing, documenting, controlling, and maintaining the settings, components, and characteristics of systems over time.

2
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:18.380
Organizations rely on configuration management to maintain consistency, reduce errors, support troubleshooting, and improve security.

3
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.960
It helps teams understand what should exist and what has changed.

4
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:30.360
Without configuration management, systems can drift away from approved states and become increasingly difficult to manage.

5
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:37.260
Small undocumented differences can become operational problems, security gaps, or audit findings.

6
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.340
In practice, configuration management connects engineering work with governance.

7
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:49.000
It gives teams a controlled way to manage change while preserving reliability, accountability, and visibility.
